    dict(key='12-act-4-figure', kind='figure', title='Keyed on the real address: the header is ignored',
         body='real_address',
         narration='Fourth demo: the same limit, counted on the real connection address. [[slnc 400]] The client cannot choose that one. [[slnc 600]] At the top, the requests. [[slnc 300]] The attacker sends the same twenty header values as before. [[slnc 300]] They are grey now, because nginx does not look at them. [[slnc 500]] The key is the address of the connection. [[slnc 300]] One attacker, one address, so one count. [[slnc 500]] At the bottom, the responses. [[slnc 300]] Six four oh ones, and fourteen four twenty nines, just like the second demo. [[slnc 600]] Behind a trusted proxy, the real address must come from a header that only that proxy sets. [[slnc 300]] And the proxy must overwrite whatever the client sent.'),
